		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T05:16:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Rework CHANGELOG to prose format, add v2.2 section\n\nRestructure the Mountain CHANGELOG from itemized bullet points to narrative prose paragraphs, improving readability while preserving all historical content. Add new v2.2 section documenting bundled-electron correctness pass including: JSON-RPC -32004 for benign 404s, deferred-no-op file watching, canonical-path comparison for Volumes mounts, Identifier field on SCM provider DTO, sky:replay-events handler, 64KB terminal ring buffer, and tree:getChildren timeout reduction.\n\nThe new format emphasizes user-facing impact over file references, making it more useful for release notes and external communication.",
			"SHA": "9515b2f72adf9866c58023f42f52630759ffa3da"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:21:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Buffer terminal output for late-listener replay\n\nAdd per-terminal output buffering to solve the same race condition that\nwas fixed for tree-views and SCM in 1599d766. The PTY reader task and\nSkyBridge's `listen(\"sky://terminal/*\")` installation race: in the\nbundled-electron profile, the shell's first prompt fires ~50ms after\n`spawn_command` while Sky's bundle still parses for ~1500ms. Without a\nbuffer, zsh MOTD, direnv exports, fish greetings are silently dropped\nand the user sees an empty pane until they type.\n\nThe implementation adds:\n- `AppendTerminalOutput()`: capture PTY bytes into a 64KB bounded buffer\n  (keeps most recent suffix to preserve the prompt)\n- `DrainTerminalOutputBuffer()`: retrieve all buffered terminal data\n- `RemoveTerminalOutputBuffer()`: clean up on terminal exit\n- Extended `sky:replay-events` to emit `sky://terminal/create` for each\n  active terminal AND replay any buffered `sky://terminal/data` bytes\n\nThis completes the replay system for all three major feature areas:\ntree-views, SCM providers, and terminals.",
			"SHA": "2fee91e5d72c7b86eb194a55de12d4d33f8aac92"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:01:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Use actual SCM provider identifier in replay, add command replay, reduce tree timeout\n\nThree improvements to Sky event replay:\n\n1. **SCM Provider Identifier**: The `ProviderState` DTO now carries the original `Identifier` field from `ProviderData.ID`. SCM replay uses this instead of hardcoded \"git\", enabling multi-SCM support (github, hg, etc.). Pre-existing DTOs default to \"git\" for backward compatibility.\n\n2. **Command Registration Replay**: Add replay for extension-registered commands (`vscode.commands.registerCommand`). Native Rust handlers are excluded since they're not exposed via the Vine notification channel. This ensures `ICommandService` knows about extension commands after bridge install.\n\n3. **Tree-View Timeout**: Reduce `$provideTreeChildren` timeout from 5000ms to 1500ms. User-interactive RPCs should show a spinner and fail gracefully — real workloads (gitlens, rust-analyzer) finish in <500ms. Slow producers fall through to empty-array and retry on scroll.\n\nExtends the sky:replay-events handler added in 1599d766.",
			"SHA": "1f93b7ef93262b34e18e1109e24268a36e2caf07"
		}
	],
